SPEAR documentation
======================

Sphinx documentation for the local LLM assistant infrastructure under
/opt/llm. Layout and build targets mirror soo/so3/doc.

Build
-----

    make html                 # -> build/html/index.html
    make latexpdf             # -> build/latex/SPEAR.pdf
    make clean

Sphinx and the RTD theme come from the system Python (/usr/bin/sphinx-build),
not from the spear virtualenv, which carries only the application's
runtime dependencies.

Diagrams
--------

    make diagrams             # regenerates source/img/spear.drawio AND the SVGs

source/img/gen_spear_diagrams.py is the single description of every diagram.
Running it writes two things from that one description:

  * spear.drawio        the editable multi-page drawio document (one page per
                        diagram) — open it in draw.io or the VS Code extension
                        and every box is editable;
  * spear_<page>.svg    the rendered diagrams the HTML build consumes.

Keep structural changes in the generator: editing the .drawio by hand works,
but a subsequent `make diagrams` regenerates it.

Why the SVGs are not exported from the .drawio
----------------------------------------------

export_png.sh drives the drawio CLI and is kept for environments where that
CLI works. On this machine it does not: the drawio snap 30.4.1 fails on every
input with

    Error reading file: <path>
    ReferenceError: next is not defined
        at processOneFile (.../app.asar/src/main/electron.js:1256:8)

including a five-element minimal file and the SO3 documentation's own
diagrams. Rendering the SVGs directly from the generator keeps the
documentation build independent of that upstream bug, and SVG stays crisp at
any zoom.

The version string
------------------

conf.py derives `release` from spear/active-model.conf, so the served
model appears in the page header and never has to be bumped by hand.
